      "content": "{\"classifications\":{\"42\":\"1\",\"50\":\"0\",\"57\":\"0\",\"89\":\"1\",\"133\":\"0\",\"157\":\"0\",\"189\":\"0\",\"214\":\"0\",\"240\":\"0\",\"299\":\"1\",\"453\":\"0\",\"490\":\"0\",\"597\":\"0\",\"630\":\"0\",\"656\":\"0\",\"714\":\"1\",\"721\":\"0\",\"744\":\"0\",\"773\":\"1\",\"794\":\"1\",\"805\":\"0\",\"817\":\"0\",\"871\":\"0\",\"873\":\"1\",\"918\":\"0\",\"964\":\"0\",\"967\":\"0\",\"1021\":\"0\",\"1043\":\"1\",\"1060\":\"1\",\"1086\":\"0\",\"1118\":\"0\",\"1139\":\"0\",\"1155\":\"1\",\"1177\":\"0\",\"1230\":\"1\",\"1257\":\"1\",\"1313\":\"0\",\"1320\":\"1\",\"1325\":\"0\",\"1610\":\"0\",\"1736\":\"0\",\"1747\":\"1\",\"1749\":\"0\",\"1827\":\"1\",\"1862\":\"1\",\"1897\":\"0\",\"1927\":\"1\",\"1957\":\"0\",\"2003\":\"0\",\"2026\":\"1\",\"2143\":\"0\",\"2318\":\"1\",\"2335\":\"1\",\"2368\":\"1\",\"2382\":\"1\",\"2627\":\"1\",\"2675\":\"0\",\"2697\":\"1\",\"2807\":\"0\",\"2827\":\"0\",\"2869\":\"0\",\"2895\":\"1\",\"3038\":\"0\",\"3047\":\"1\",\"3143\":\"1\",\"3149\":\"1\",\"3201\":\"1\",\"3252\":\"1\",\"3271\":\"1\",\"3477\":\"0\",\"3482\":\"1\",\"3501\":\"0\",\"3534\":\"0\",\"3560\":\"0\",\"3577\":\"1\",\"3659\":\"0\",\"3687\":\"0\",\"3729\":\"1\",\"3744\":\"0\",\"3817\":\"0\",\"3845\":\"0\",\"3914\":\"0\",\"3950\":\"0\",\"4022\":\"0\",\"4122\":\"1\",\"4124\":\"0\",\"4184\":\"0\",\"4207\":\"0\",\"4208\":\"0\",\"4295\":\"0\",\"4328\":\"1\",\"4344\":\"0\",\"4403\":\"1\",\"4508\":\"1\",\"4531\":\"1\",\"4585\":\"1\",\"4677\":\"0\",\"4771\":\"1\",\"4774\":\"1\"},\"codebook\":{\"definition\":\"Credit-claiming occurs when a senator presents themself as having helped cause, obtain, protect, enact, fund, or otherwise deliver a concrete government action, policy outcome, resource, or benefit.\",\"clarification\":\"Classify a release as credit-claiming when it explicitly links the senator's own action or leadership to a realized or advancing outcome. Relevant actions include securing appropriations or grants, authoring provisions enacted or included in legislation, obtaining an agency decision, influencing an administrative action, or successfully protecting a local facility or program. Joint claims by a delegation count when the senator is identified as participating in the successful effort. A claim may concern benefits for a state, locality, organization, or broader public.\",\"positive_examples\":[{\"text\":\"Sen. Talent announced that the Senate has approved his request for $1.5 million dollars for the Health Sciences Research and Education Facility at the University of Missouri-Columbia.\",\"explanation\":\"This explicitly attributes approved funding to Talent's request, claiming a role in delivering a concrete resource to a Missouri institution.\"},{\"text\":\"Dorgan authored legislation, which was signed into law, that created the National Center designation.\",\"explanation\":\"The release ties the college's newly received designation to legislation Dorgan authored and that became law.\"},{\"text\":\"The announcement follows the Senator's Monday appeal to President Bush to authorize the immediate transport of available trailers staged outside the Katrina disaster area.\",\"explanation\":\"The release connects Lott's appeal to FEMA's announced movement of temporary housing for Mississippi hurricane victims.\"}],\"negative_clarification\":\"Do not classify a release as credit-claiming when it only states a policy position, criticizes another official or administration, commemorates an event or person, announces a grant without asserting senatorial involvement, or describes a request, bill introduction, cosponsorship, meeting, or future intention without claiming a concrete result. Praise for another actor's accomplishment is also not self-credit-claiming.\",\"negative_examples\":[{\"text\":\"The Bush Administration's 'head in the sand' position on global warming has defied reason and common sense.\",\"explanation\":\"This is criticism of the administration's policy, not a claim that Senator Reid delivered a policy result or benefit.\"},{\"text\":\"Senator Allard will hold a town meeting in Greeley on Wednesday January 12.\",\"explanation\":\"This is an event announcement and invitation, with no assertion of having secured or delivered an outcome.\"},{\"text\":\"Sen. Salazar announced that he has joined a bipartisan group of colleagues in support of the compromise reached between the Senate and the White House on the PATRIOT Act.\",\"explanation\":\"Joining or supporting a compromise expresses a stance, but the release does not claim that Salazar obtained or delivered the compromise or a concrete benefit.\"}]}}",
